WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.574 --> 00:00:17.636
knew that she had done the right thing by contacting Rose, but a part of her regretted her

2
00:00:17.736 --> 00:00:22.299
actions. She felt bitter toward Fagin for leading her into a life of crime.

3
00:00:23.299 --> 00:00:26.561
Yet she still didn't want to be the one who brought him within the grasp of the police.

4
00:00:27.722 --> 00:00:31.504
As for Bill Sikes, she had dropped no clues that could lead to his discovery.

5
00:00:32.544 --> 00:00:35.265
For his sake she had refused Rose's offers of sanctuary.

6
00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:37.926
She had done all she could for Sikes.

7
00:00:38.986 --> 00:00:40.467
She had done the right thing for Oliver.

8
00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:46.469
Although she came to this same conclusion whenever she thought about the situation, Nancy still felt uneasy.

9
00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:49.930
She quickly grew pale and thin with anxiety.

10
00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.671
It was Sunday night at Bill Sikes' house.

11
00:00:53.831 --> 00:00:56.492
Nancy sat silent and dejected with her head in her hands.

12
00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:02.161
When the clock on the nearest church struck the hour, Nancy raised her head, remembering how she'd told

13
00:01:02.221 --> 00:01:04.482
Rose to look for her on London Bridge on Sunday nights.

14
00:01:04.502 --> 00:01:08.123
"It's eleven o'clock," said Sikes.

15
00:01:09.263 --> 00:01:11.084
He went to the window and peeked through the shutter.

16
00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.184
"A dark night too.

17
00:01:14.225 --> 00:01:15.925
A good night for some illegal business."

18
00:01:17.025 --> 00:01:21.507
"What a pity, Bill, my dear," said Fagin, "that there's none quite ready to be done.

19
00:01:22.587 --> 00:01:25.028
We need to plan another robbery now that you're feeling better."

20
00:01:26.148 --> 00:01:29.089
"Yes, we must make up for lost time," said Sikes.

21
00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:32.089
"It does me good to hear you talk like that."

22
00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.130
Fagin reached over and patted him on the shoulder.

23
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.791
"You're quite like yourself again."

24
00:01:38.791 --> 00:01:40.832
They bantered back and forth, ignoring Nancy.

25
00:01:41.812 --> 00:01:44.833
Taking advantage of this, she put on her bonnet and started to go out.

26
00:01:45.793 --> 00:01:48.554
But Fagin suddenly noticed her and pulled on Sikes' sleeve.

27
00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.215
"Hold on, Nancy!"

28
00:01:51.555 --> 00:01:52.195
cried Sikes.

29
00:01:52.215 --> 00:01:54.775
"Where are you going at this time of night?"

30
00:01:55.876 --> 00:01:56.396
"Not far."

31
00:01:57.472 --> 00:01:58.553
"What kind of answer is that?

32
00:01:59.653 --> 00:02:00.594
Tell me where you're going."

33
00:02:01.694 --> 00:02:03.576
"I don't know where," replied Nancy.

34
00:02:03.596 --> 00:02:05.196
"Then I do.

35
00:02:06.197 --> 00:02:07.097
You're going nowhere.

36
00:02:08.138 --> 00:02:08.638
Sit down."

37
00:02:09.719 --> 00:02:13.321
Sikes said this more out of stubbornness than because he really objected to her going out.

38
00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:15.062
"I'm not well.

39
00:02:16.062 --> 00:02:16.643
You know that.

40
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:18.584
I want a breath of air."

41
00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.865
"Stick your head out the window."

42
00:02:20.885 --> 00:02:23.347
"I can't get enough air that way.

43
00:02:24.427 --> 00:02:25.608
I need to go out on the street."

44
00:02:26.584 --> 00:02:27.665
"You're not going out."

45
00:02:28.765 --> 00:02:30.446
Sikes crossed the room and locked the door.

46
00:02:31.427 --> 00:02:34.728
Then he pulled Nancy's bonnet from her head and flung it on top of an old chest.

47
00:02:34.748 --> 00:02:39.011
"Lack of a bonnet won't keep me inside," Nancy said angrily.

48
00:02:39.031 --> 00:02:41.232
"Do you know what you're doing, Bill?"

49
00:02:41.252 --> 00:02:43.873
"Know what I'm doing?"

50
00:02:44.253 --> 00:02:45.274
Sikes turned to Fagin.

51
00:02:46.295 --> 00:02:49.076
"She must be out of her senses or she wouldn't dare talk to me that way."

52
00:02:49.096 --> 00:02:52.578
"You'll drive me to something desperate," Nancy threatened.

53
00:02:52.598 --> 00:02:54.719
"Let me go this minute!"

54
00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.305
"No!" shouted Sikes.

55
00:02:57.325 --> 00:03:01.008
"Tell him to let me go, Fagin," Nancy said pleadingly.

56
00:03:02.089 --> 00:03:06.833
Fagin continued to watch the scene in silence, wondering why Nancy needed to go out right that minute.

57
00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.615
"Bill, you really don't know what you're doing!"

58
00:03:09.975 --> 00:03:11.297
Nancy said with great force.

59
00:03:12.397 --> 00:03:14.319
Then she sat down on the floor in front of the door.

60
00:03:14.339 --> 00:03:16.841
"Let me go for only an hour."

61
00:03:16.861 --> 00:03:19.423
"I think the girl's gone insane!"

62
00:03:19.804 --> 00:03:20.384
said Sikes.

63
00:03:21.485 --> 00:03:22.306
"Get up, Nancy."

64
00:03:23.327 --> 00:03:24.668
But Nancy refused to move.

65
00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.009
Sikes grabbed her and dragged her off to another room.

66
00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:33.952
There he held her captive until the church clock struck midnight and she stopped trying to escape.

67
00:03:35.092 --> 00:03:37.093
Leaving her to recover, he returned to Fagin.

68
00:03:37.113 --> 00:03:40.534
"Why do you think she took it into her head to go out tonight?"

69
00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:41.395
Bill asked.

70
00:03:42.515 --> 00:03:43.396
Fagin shook his head.

71
00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:46.337
"Woman's stubbornness, I suppose, my dear."

72
00:03:47.377 --> 00:03:50.539
As he uttered these words, Nancy reappeared and took her former seat.

73
00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:53.660
"It's time for me to leave," said Fagin.

74
00:03:54.688 --> 00:03:57.911
"Could someone bring a light so I don't fall downstairs and break my neck?"

75
00:03:59.032 --> 00:04:00.913
"Show him out, Nancy," said Sikes.

76
00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.176
Nancy followed Fagin downstairs with a candle.

77
00:04:05.197 --> 00:04:08.900
When they reached the front door, he turned to her and said, "What's the matter, dear?"

78
00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.621
"What do you mean?"

79
00:04:11.742 --> 00:04:12.903
Fagin whispered in her ear.

80
00:04:12.923 --> 00:04:16.106
"He treats you worse than he treats his dog.

81
00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:19.128
If you ever want revenge, come to me."

82
00:04:19.148 --> 00:04:23.612
"Good night," said Nancy without showing any emotion.

83
00:04:24.732 --> 00:04:27.373
She shrank back as Fagin tried to pat her hand.

84
00:04:28.474 --> 00:04:31.255
Fagin walked toward home, thinking about what he had just seen.

85
00:04:31.275 --> 00:04:35.777
"Nancy must have fallen in love with someone else," he said to himself.

86
00:04:35.797 --> 00:04:38.678
"That's why she's acting so strangely."

87
00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:41.359
He began to think of an evil plot.

88
00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.521
If he could get Nancy to poison Sikes, that would benefit them both.

89
00:04:46.781 --> 00:04:48.982
She'd no longer be subjected to Sikes' cruelty.

90
00:04:49.963 --> 00:04:52.424
He'd no longer have to worry that Sikes might turn against him.

91
00:04:53.472 --> 00:04:56.093
"The man I hate would be gone," Fagin said.

92
00:04:56.113 --> 00:05:00.815
"And I'd have unlimited power over Nancy because I'd know that she killed him."

93
00:05:01.876 --> 00:05:04.517
But Nancy might recoil from the idea of killing Sikes.

94
00:05:05.657 --> 00:05:07.658
"How can I increase my influence over her?"

95
00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:10.279
Fagin wondered as he arrived home.

96
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.561
And suddenly he thought of another plan.

97
00:05:14.661 --> 00:05:17.542
He would send someone to spy on her and catch her with her new love.

98
00:05:18.623 --> 00:05:22.228
Then he could threaten to reveal this information to Sikes.

99
00:05:22.248 --> 00:05:24.269
"She won't be able to refuse my request then."

100
00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.111
Fagin rubbed his hands together with glee.

101
00:05:28.212 --> 00:05:31.935
The next morning Fagin was up early, waiting for a new member of his gang to appear at

102
00:05:31.955 --> 00:05:32.735
the breakfast table.

103
00:05:33.936 --> 00:05:36.257
At last the new boy, Bolter, sat down.

104
00:05:37.398 --> 00:05:38.559
Fagin leaned over the table.

105
00:05:38.579 --> 00:05:43.923
"Bolter, I want you to do a piece of work for me that requires great care and caution."

106
00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.864
"Is it dangerous?"

107
00:05:46.945 --> 00:05:48.566
Bolter looked over his cup of coffee.

108
00:05:49.706 --> 00:05:51.728
"No, you only have to follow a young woman."

109
00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:54.589
"I can do that," said the boy.

110
00:05:54.609 --> 00:05:57.591
"I was a regular sneak when I was at school.

111
00:05:58.712 --> 00:05:59.792
Why am I following her?"

112
00:05:59.812 --> 00:06:05.736
"Just to tell me where she goes, whom she meets, and if possible what she says."

113
00:06:05.756 --> 00:06:07.617
"Who is she?"

114
00:06:07.637 --> 00:06:10.259
"One of us who has gone astray."

115
00:06:11.359 --> 00:06:12.600
Fagin got up from the table.

116
00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.902
"I'll tell you where to find her."

117
00:06:16.082 --> 00:06:18.664
After that Bolter was ready to shadow the woman every day.

118
00:06:19.724 --> 00:06:23.465
But it was not until late Sunday night that Fagin finally summoned him to a pub.

119
00:06:23.485 --> 00:06:26.066
"There," whispered Fagin.

120
00:06:26.086 --> 00:06:27.926
"Do you see her?"

121
00:06:28.967 --> 00:06:29.707
Bolter nodded.

122
00:06:30.727 --> 00:06:34.748
They were hidden behind a small glass panel that enabled them to look down into a room behind

123
00:06:34.788 --> 00:06:35.169
the bar.

124
00:06:36.309 --> 00:06:38.910
After a few minutes, the woman got up and left the pub.

125
00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:41.590
"Go!" Fagin nudged Bolter.

126
00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:46.452
"She turned left," said one of Fagin's minions standing at the door to the pub.

127
00:06:47.552 --> 00:06:51.000
Bolter stepped out into the dark street and began to follow Nancy.
